From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iván Ruiz <iruizl2004@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:44:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: apply the Surface Pro 11 speaker settings to the
 LCD model too

The wsa884x 2S/4 ohm profile (2154) and the raised speaker volume
ceiling (2147) were gated to microsoft,denali-oled, the X Elite OLED
tree. The LCD Surface Pro 11 (X Plus, microsoft,denali-lcd) has the same
speakers: its amplifiers report the 2S VPHX supply configuration, and
Windows drives them with the same Dolby tuning, whose hardware ID on
that machine is AUCD\VEN_QCOM&DEV_0C29&SUBSYS_MSHW0486&REV_0D, as on
the OLED. On the LCD tree it would fall back to the 1S defaults and the
upstream -3 dB/0 dB caps.

Gate both on microsoft,denali, which both trees carry.

Assisted-by: LLM

---
 sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c | 7 ++++---
 sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c  | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
index eb138ab..ad846d5 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
@@ -1635,11 +1635,12 @@ static void wsa884x_init(struct wsa884x_priv *wsa884x)
 		wsa884x->supply_config = supply_config;
 		/*
 		 * The 2S settings below include the Surface Pro 11's 4 ohm
-		 * load policy, so other boards keep the upstream 1S defaults
-		 * until their speakers are characterised.
+		 * load policy (OLED and LCD models alike), so other boards
+		 * keep the upstream 1S defaults until their speakers are
+		 * characterised.
 		 */
 		if (supply_config == WSA884X_SUPPLY_2S &&
-		    !of_machine_is_compatible("microsoft,denali-oled")) {
+		    !of_machine_is_compatible("microsoft,denali")) {
 			wsa884x->supply_config = WSA884X_SUPPLY_1S;
 			dev_info(wsa884x->dev,
 				 "VPHX supply configuration is 2S; retaining upstream 1S defaults on this board\n");
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c b/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c
index 0d32f02..c76e2d5 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c
@@ -53,7 +53,7 @@ static int x1e80100_snd_init(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd)
 		 * would buy nothing; the digital cap was what held a full-scale
 		 * signal 3 dB short of the amplifiers' full scale.
 		 */
-		if (of_machine_is_compatible("microsoft,denali-oled")) {
+		if (of_machine_is_compatible("microsoft,denali")) {
 			digital_max = 84;
 			pa_max = 12;
 		} else if (of_machine_is_compatible("asus,zenbook-a16-ux3607oa")) {
-- 
